Faster Debug

Run:

Shell
docker run --rm \
-v ~/prometheus/prometheus.yml:/etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml \
prom/prometheus \
--config.file=/etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml

This will validate the YAML and show the exact line causing the failure.

Check Your YAML

Your screenshot looked visually correct, but Linux Prometheus is very sensitive.

Run:

Shell
cat ~/prometheus/prometheus.yml

The file should look exactly like:

YAML
global:
scrape_interval: 15s
 
scrape_configs:
- job_name: "prometheus"
static_configs:
- targets:
- "localhost:9090"
 
- job_name: "node-exporter"
static_configs:
- targets:
- "172.17.0.1:9100"
Important

Replace:

YAML
host.docker.internal:9100

with:

YAML
172.17.0.1:9100

On Linux, host.docker.internal often does not work inside containers.

Verify File Before Starting

Run:

Shell
cat ~/prometheus/prometheus.yml

and make sure every level has proper spaces.

